{"type":"result","subtype":"success","is_error":false,"api_error_status":null,"duration_ms":23840,"duration_api_ms":24925,"num_turns":8,"result":"I wrote `src/cpufreq/cpufreq.bt`, but I haven't run it. The sandbox blocked every `bpftrace` command, so even the tracepoint check didn't run.\n\nIt attaches to the `power:cpu_frequency` tracepoint. For each frequency change it prints the time, CPU, old and new MHz, and the delta. On Ctrl-C it also prints:\n- `@changes`: number of changes per CPU.\n- `@time_at_freq_ms`: milliseconds spent at each frequency, per CPU.\n- `@freq_mhz`: a histogram of frequencies.\n\nOn some systems the tracepoint doesn't fire. That happens with `intel_pstate` in active mode and with hardware-managed P-states. Switching to `acpi-cpufreq` or `intel_pstate=passive` should make it fire.\n\nRun it with `sudo bpftrace src/cpufreq/cpufreq.bt`. Tell me if you'd rather it live somewhere else in the repo, or want a README or Makefile for it.","stop_reason":"end_turn","session_id":"b0bae2dd-36e1-4e6f-a95f-7480c0ae984c","total_cost_usd":0.12805055,"usage":{"input_tokens":14,"cache_creation_input_tokens":14331,"cache_read_input_tokens":144071,"output_tokens":2040,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":14331},"inference_geo":"","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":347,"cache_read_input_tokens":27091,"cache_creation_input_tokens":968,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":968,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"modelUsage":{"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001":{"inputTokens":351,"outputTokens":19,"cacheReadInputTokens":0,"cacheCreationInputTokens":0,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":0.000446,"contextWindow":200000,"maxOutputTokens":32000},"claude-sonnet-5-5":{"inputTokens":14,"outputTokens":2040,"cacheReadInputTokens":144071,"cacheCreationInputTokens":14331,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":